§ `s 50(12) -- cancelling an application`

`an applicant who innocently misstated her income` MEANS `Application facts` WITH
    `I made a material misrepresentation or false statement, even innocently` IS TRUE
    `one of us was convicted of a killer-litter offence from Board property` IS FALSE
    `I failed to return a CPF cash grant when required` IS FALSE
    `one of us was convicted of harbouring an immigration offender` IS FALSE

`an applicant with nothing against her` MEANS `Application facts` WITH
    `I made a material misrepresentation or false statement, even innocently` IS FALSE
    `one of us was convicted of a killer-litter offence from Board property` IS FALSE
    `I failed to return a CPF cash grant when required` IS FALSE
    `one of us was convicted of harbouring an immigration offender` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `Can the Board cancel my application to buy a flat` `an applicant who innocently misstated her income`
#ASSERT NOT `Can the Board cancel my application to buy a flat` `an applicant with nothing against her`

